# `exit` ends the shell, and `init` starts a new one in the same terminal: the
# machine stays on (ADR-0155's Decision, INV-0155-5, INV-0155-6).
! panicked
! first process ended
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n/> 
# The first exit with a job running only warns; the second ends both.
> sleep 60 &\r
< [1] sleep 60
< \r\n/> 
> exit\r
< 1 job is still running; exit again to end it
< \r\n/> 
# Anything else between the two starts the count again.
> echo between\r
< \r\nbetween
< \r\n/> 
> exit\r
< 1 job is still running; exit again to end it
< \r\n/> 
> exit\r
< init: shell ended: ExitRecord { code: 0, reason: Exited
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n/> 
# A new shell: no jobs, and it runs commands.
> jobs\r
x [1]
< \r\n/> 
> echo again\r
< \r\nagain
< \r\n/> 
> exit\r
< init: shell ended
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n/> 
x power off
> poweroff\r
